@Rubenisme thanks for contacting us.

It seems we closed the other issue ahead of time, sorry about that. Some times we mark them as answered early and our bot closes them before we can re-evaluate them.

Seems like we would need to implement IDisposable [here](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/a9a6831a1a0aa2fc21c276e1f28b86a2b1cdbb28/src/Hosting/TestHost/src/ClientHandler.cs)

@Tratcher are you ok with this change? It would help people catch errors when the HttpClient instance gets disposed before you are done with it.

> For reference, what kind of HttpContent is it?

@Tratcher or @JamesNK, just so you are aware, there is a [GH repo](https://github.com/Rubenisme/reproduce-request-disposed) mentioned in the first issue for easy testing of this.

I understand the focus this summer on the coming release, though hope it can be picked up quickly afterwards.
